--
--   **Context.** Round six, item language (I3): allocating the temporaries
--
--   The complex network acts on `W` data/scratch roles and `T` temporaries (`Fin (W + T)`, data
--   first).  At a node the stream holds the `W` data roles (`W n` records); `padCU xL xQ U` appends
--   `T n` zero records (the clean temporaries), runs the role program `U` on `W + T` roles, and drops
--   the temporaries again.  Only the data block of the network operator matters (`DataCorrect`), since
--   the temporaries enter as zeros and leave unread.
--
--   * `flatR_eq_of_getD`, `exists_flatR`, `flatR_append`, `flatR_padX`, `flatR_take_castAdd`;
--   * `roleOpF_padX`: the data rows of `roleOpF` on zero-padded temporaries;
--   * **`sImplQ_padRole`**: `padCU xL xQ U` implements the data block `Tm` on `W n` records.
